WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.610
T-This church is...

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.780
This weird twining of the ivy...

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.730
It looks just like Manager’s head!

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.700
That’s the place that led to
you getting that hair style, right?

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.290
Those words of Tsukino...

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.870
It might just be that there’s some sort of

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:26.730
weird karma between Manager and this church.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.500
Hello.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.510
Do you have any business with St. Andrew’s Church?

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.760
Umm... No, I...

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.560
Well, well, well, well, well...

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.890
Let’s not stand here talking.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:40.100
Come on inside. Come on.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.850
Come, come, come, come in.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:42.890
P-P-Please wait.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.230
You find something unsatisfactory?

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.320
No, it’s not unsatisfactory, but...

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.240
I did come in search of this place, but...

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.240
After seeing such a strangely shaped church,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.450
I’ve begun to question whether or
not coming here was really a good idea.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.950
Attention!

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.330
Be not deceived by what the eyes perceive.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.800
While this church may appear to be
of a suspicious nature in your eyes,

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.340
that is only because there is a devil twisting

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.050
its appearance nested within your heart.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:18.640
What? I don’t understand what you’re saying at all.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.640
Well, well, well, well...

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.310
That and this, and everything
will be explained inside at leisure.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.020
W-Wait. Umm...
That and this, and everything
will be explained inside at leisure.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.980
W-Wait. Umm...

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.400
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.320
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.650
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:38.060
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:43.290
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:47.130
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:04.110
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:12.080
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:19.950
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:27.670
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:35.140
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:44.520
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:53.280
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:57.540
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.530
is the light of only you.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:04.280
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:09.090
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:16.810
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.510
The sticky showdown!!

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.310
Azuma Kazuma vs Kanmuri Shigeru!

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.680
Wh-Why are you locking the door?

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.280
Okay. With this, we can relax.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.070
Wh-What do you mean relax?

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:46.080
It’s even more suspicious
than before. Now it’s even scary!

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.200
No, no, no, no, no.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.790
I just wonder how many years
it’s been since a believer came here.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.960
O Lord!

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.040
I thank thee.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.290
Exactly when did she decide I was a believer?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.550
Come, my lost lamb.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.470
There’s no need to be afraid any more.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:02.840
You’re the one making me lost and afraid!

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.260
The Lord will encompass everything about you.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.390
No...

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.690
Well, I don’t really care about God and such things.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:11.770
Well, well, well, well.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.900
There’s no need to be ashamed of your piety.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.820
You must be honest to your heart.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:19.020
For now, let’s start with a confession, shall we?

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.400
I don’t need it!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.740
Even without that, I will...

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:23.580
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.
Even without that, I will...

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:24.530
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.500
W-Wait!

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.790
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.880
All right. Now...

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.500
confess all your sins to date.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:40.000
Wh-What’s with this turn of events...?

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:44.020
Be not afraid of confessing your sins.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.390
Should you truly repent within your heart,

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:52.770
the Lord will forgive this, and that, and even those...

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:56.520
He will forgive all your sins.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.320
Oh, is that so?

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.030
But, I haven’t committed any particular sin...

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:09.130
As I thought. You have indeed committed some sin.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:14.000
But, there is no need to fear.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.710
Humans are sinful beings by nature.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.170
Gather your courage and confess.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:22.010
The Lord will forgive you for sure.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:26.010
I don’t really believe in God, but...

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:30.010
If I confess about that time, I might feel a little better.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:32.390
Hey.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.810
Success! Rolling pin slip plan, bingo!

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.570
I stepped on something and fell.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.580
I’m begging you, it’s my life’s request.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.540
If I cannot remain after this exam, I...

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.240
My little brother and sister...

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:57.880
Is this guy a moron?

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.330
Number 34, Kawachi-kun.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:05.090
I have decided to recruit you
to Pantasia’s main Tokyo store.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:06.970
Oh...

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:07.720
U-Um...

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:15.020
Actually... When I took the
Pantasia recruitment exam...

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.350
What was that?!

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:23.150
While it may have been for your family,
when you took the exam for that bakery,

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.150
in order to flunk a person
named Azuma-san,

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.780
on top of stepping on and destroying some <i>Japan</i> #56,

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:32.240
you deceived that naive Azuma person and

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.100
passed his achievement off as your own?!

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.250
Ye... Yeah.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.460
And on top of that,

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.960
you’re saying that you’re having this
person take your revenge for you?!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.920
Uh. Yeah.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:44.590
And on TOP of that,

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:48.010
even though you’re not a believer, you
deceived me and received a confessional.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:51.430
And in addition, you come here to ask for

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:55.040
the Church’s help as you cannot
win with your own skill. Preposterous!

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:59.000
The verdict is that you are the dregs of humanity.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:06:59.690
The dregs?

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.440
Even the Lord would not be able to forgive this...

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.150
You pig.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.490
P-Pig...?

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:08.450
I’m on the same level as Umino Katsuo?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.160
But, earlier you said that the
Lord would forgive anything!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.120
Moreover, I had no intentions of deceiving you!

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:25.470
You mistook me for a believer all by yourself!

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:29.680
But then...

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.930
if you were to lose
in the third place match,

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:37.720
it’s also a fact that Yukino, an even greater villain than you, will have taken a lead.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.350
It can’t be helped.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.650
I will cooperate with you.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.940
Re-Really?

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.270
In that case, let’s get the Father...

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.780
Ah, about that...

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:49.900
I have to refuse your request.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:52.280
Father Graham, whom you
wished to see, is...

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:56.960
no longer in this world.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.410
He has risen to the heavens.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.880
Wh... What?!

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:12.720
So, what in the world are you going to do, Azuma-san?

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:16.060
With the petalite board
having disappeared...

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:19.180
won’t it be an obstacle for
baking the bread in the finals?

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:22.560
No. Actually, this may have been
for the best.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:23.480
What?

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.730
Actually, that board was my second one.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.950
When I first had a board made...

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:33.830
Delicious!!

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:37.330
This is a truly delicious bread, Kazuma!

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:41.170
I went to heaven and was
having fun there with the ladies!

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:42.200
Really. This is delicious.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.840
I must thank Umasaburou as well.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:47.420
Yeah!

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:53.180
As long as I have this board,
I can make a delicious <i>Japan</i> anytime.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.140
Yeah.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.560
At that time, I really thought so,

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.100
and got caught up in the moment.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:03.350
I depended on the board to
make <i>Japan</i> #44 day after day.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.190
How is it? Is it good Grandpa?

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.970
It’s good, but...

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.190
But... everyone was...

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:13.780
I’m beginning to get tired of having this everyday.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:17.200
Won’t you make #43 once in a while?

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.370
No... No way!

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.170
At that time, I realized it.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:29.210
No matter how delicious something is,
you get sick of it if you eat it every day.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:36.260
So, I have to come up with various
tricks, and make all kinds of breads. Right?

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:40.680
I don’t think Dave or Kuroyanagi

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.620
would go to heaven again if they were to eat it either.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.480
So...

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:48.970
So, I’ll make a new bread again.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:52.730
The new <i>Japan</i> #60!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.990
And we take on the finals with that!

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.710
You seem to be doing
something awesome there, aren’t you?

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:11.720
You developing some kind of chemical weapon?

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:12.930
Of course not.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.890
Taiensei reinforcing yeast.

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:17.800
It’s the Kaiyou yeast RAS.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.060
Taiensei? RAS?

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:23.760
What’s that?

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:29.070
Salt is extremely important in adding taste to all food,

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.770
including bread.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.200
But, the yeast used regularly for bread,

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:38.280
Saccharomyces cerevisiae,
has a very low endurance to salt.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.660
That is, it’s weak against salt content.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:45.290
When you add salt to the dough, it
can no longer work to its full capacity.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:49.210
But, this new Kaiyou yeast, RAS,

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.290
has resilience against salt.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:56.220
As these yeasts were living in sea water,

00:10:56.220 --> 00:11:01.850
they’re relatively resistant to salt.

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:03.560
And by further reinforcing this characteristic,

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.900
we have improved the bread yeast so that it can work to 100% capacity,

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:09.020
even if you add salt to the dough.
And that’s what it is.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.100
Uh, she’s not there.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.320
Sounds boring.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.490
Are you going to continue?

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.490
Uh, no.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:25.330
I explained only because you asked.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.500
You sow!

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:29.250
Oh, whatever.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.040
Explaining anything more
than this to an amateur is no use.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.500
It would be like casting pearls before swine.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:36.800
Either way,

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:41.470
if we were to give bread the ability to
ferment and absorb water to 100% capacity,

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:44.020
we would be able to create a dough with

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:48.690
supreme elasticity and strength for the first time.

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:52.520
A dough with the sticky
consistency that the Japanese really like.

00:11:55.240 --> 00:12:00.500
Azuma-kun’s petalite board or my Kaiyou yeast RAS.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:04.160
Let’s see which one is superior at the finals.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.250
Aaah, so busy, so busy!

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:09.750
Manager has gone off somewhere as usual.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.380
In addition, Kawachi-kun has gone off
for confession at some church somewhere.

00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:16.340
Azuma-kun is busy with
research for a bread for the finals.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:20.130
And to top it off, Tsukino-san is
constantly by Azuma-kun’s side.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:22.600
It’s truly tragic!

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.890
Tsukino-san with Azuma-kun...

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.140
No! Please! Please stop.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:32.180
It’s all right this way.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:33.890
A-Azuma!

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.150
Stop. Please stop.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:38.530
It’s all right.

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:39.780
It’s all right this way.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:41.530
No!!

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:45.530
What are you doing, Azuma-kun?!

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:50.170
If you do that, the bread will... The bread will...

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:54.540
What are you doing? To my Tsukino-san?

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:55.920
It’s all right.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.460
It’s all right this way.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.960
This is how we’ll make <i>Japan</i> #60.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.410
How we’ll make <i>Japan</i> #60...?

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:04.720
Yeah.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:08.060
<i>Japan</i> #60 will be a sticky bread.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:09.980
A sticky bread...?

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.000
All right. In 30 minutes, at 10:00 a.m.,

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:37.000
the finals of the 39th
Pantasia Newcomers’ Battle will begin!

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:41.210
From the Shinjuku Central Branch,
Kanmuri Shigeru!

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.510
From the Southern Tokyo Branch,
Azuma Kazuma!

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.720
Combatants, begin your preparations.

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.470
Good luck to both of you!

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.730
Make a good bread!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.440
There’s a lot of people...

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:04.190
It’s true that every year the
finals draw a big crowd, but...

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:05.690
to think that it would be so many...

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.450
This is the reason.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:14.410
Reporters who came to the
semifinals put it into an article.

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:18.830
It’s human nature to want to come see
a bread that’s delicious enough to die for.

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.800
That may be true...

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:25.050
but, Azuma-san no longer has that board.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:29.260
Should he completely betray the audience’s hopes,

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:31.390
it’ll be a repeat of what happened with Kawachi, huh?

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.050
Yes.

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:36.900
In Kawachi’s case, it was because of
someone’s interference and manipulation.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:40.310
If he’d been able to show his skills, he should have been able to make a decent bread.

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:46.200
Anyway, there’s nothing more we can do.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:49.330
He seems to have thought something up.

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:52.450
For now, we have to just believe in him.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.000
Yes.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:56.790
Yo.

00:14:56.790 --> 00:15:01.000
From that expression, it appears you
have nothing to worry about, Azuma-kun?

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:02.750
Is that so?

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.210
Is it because of that famous board
of yours? That composure of yours...

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:08.260
My famous board?

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.470
You don’t have to pretend.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:16.270
The board you used to make the bread
that sent Kuroyanagi-senpai to heaven.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:17.980
Ah. That...

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.980
I’m not going to use that in the finals.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.070
No, I can’t use it.

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.190
Because it disappeared.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.650
It disappeared?

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:28.780
Yeah.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:30.030
After the semifinals,

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:33.580
when I realized that I’d forgotten the
board in the oven, I returned to pick it up.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:36.620
But, at that time, it was no longer...

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:40.120
That was pretty careless of you.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.460
It can’t be!

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:44.170
I told her so much not to interfere with the finals, yet...

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.720
That woman!

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:50.510
Oh, calling me pretty.
Gee, you’re really good.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.880
To catch an ordinary girl like myself...

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.890
Are you done talking?

00:15:55.390 --> 00:16:00.810
Anyway, a tall woman took
that board away somewhere.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.890
That’s why it disappeared. That’s all.

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:05.730
We have nothing more
to discuss with you.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.580
Let’s go, Azuma-san.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.490
Oh well. The culprit is probably my boss.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:16.240
After all, that’s the only thing we can think of, right?

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:21.460
I told her not to interfere, but...

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:22.670
Is it all right?

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.930
For you to make such a thoughtless statement?

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:30.710
I’m not hanging around with
that woman because I like it.

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:34.600
Well then, Azuma-kun.

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:37.430
Sadly, that board has disappeared.

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:39.850
And yet, you’re very composed.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.430
Do you have some sort of secret plan?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.440
Of course.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:48.400
Even if I can’t make <i>Japan</i> #44,
I still have <i>Japan</i> #60.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:49.820
I won’t lose to you.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.490
I feel reassured after hearing that.

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:55.280
I’ll go with all I have as well.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.280
Let’s both do our best.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:58.330
All right!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.500
Just as you’d expect from the man who’s supposed

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:07.500
to have made a bread delicious enough to die for.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:11.090
He doesn’t even quiver at losing his board.
That’s some amazing confidence.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:16.970
But... that weird name <i>Japan</i>.
I wonder if it means Japan’s bread...

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:19.350
I’ll ask him after the match is over.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:26.230
What were you talking about with the cockroaches?

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.980
A little talk about the nature of society.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.440
The only cockroach here is you.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.410
Oh yeah.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:38.160
I’ve placed a demolition team on standby
at your research facility.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:39.740
A bomb?!

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.960
It’s insurance!

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.540
In case you lose, of course.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.750
And should you betray me,
you know what will happen...

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.250
You understand, right?

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:49.710
In addition to the yeast,

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:54.970
all my research data, second only to
my life in importance, is collected there.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:57.980
No matter what, she’s not
going to allow me to go against her.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:17:59.720
This sow!

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:04.470
Should I transmit a certain
code from this cell phone... Boom!

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.430
Bomb voyage.

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:13.480
Hey, Manager.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:17.530
Why is he on the side of someone that he doesn’t like?

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:19.490
Probably the money.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.290
Money?

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:24.710
Yeast, wheat flour and chemical seasoning.

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:26.250
While the bread may disappear in one bite,

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:29.500
a great deal of funding is
required for scientific research.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:32.750
And an individual can’t come up
with that kind of funding by himself.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:35.810
Research scientists have it pretty hard, huh?

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:42.600
Come to think of it, you were also like that in the past,

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.890
Kuroyanagi...

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:47.570
Kuroyanagi-san. It’s almost 10:00 a.m.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:49.690
Very well.

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:53.900
We now begin the finals of the
39th Pantasia Newcomers’ Battle.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:55.230
Both of you, step to the counter.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.540
Begin the finals!

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.170
Azuma-kun.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:15.880
I have nothing against you, but...

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:17.970
I can’t afford to lose either.

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:19.380
I’m going to win.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:27.680
With the pan au rustique created with these
Solar Hands and the Kaiyou yeast RAS.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:33.190
That’s absurd!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.980
That’s too much water for the amount of flour in there.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:36.380
It’s not just that.

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:37.480
This is sea water.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:43.410
It’s Kaiyoushinsousui, a mineral rich
water drawn from a depth of greater

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.120
than 350 meters in the Pacific Ocean.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:51.210
The salt content of this sea water would
normally reduce the efficiency of yeast.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.710
But, the RAS, which is resilient to salt,

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.500
won’t care about this absurd amount of water.

00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:01.930
And, this salt-rich water will bestow upon bread

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:07.510
the moist, sticky, spongy
consistency that the Japanese love.

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:10.690
It’s physically impossible to create a
dough of this level using other techniques.

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:14.770
No matter how much you struggle,
you have no chance of winning this...

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:19.110
What’s he doing?!

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.110
It’s not just that the water is too much!

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:24.110
He’s washing the dough he’s kneaded with water.

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:25.950
N-No way!

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:30.580
If you do that, the starch of the
dough will dissolve and it will break up.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.130
Azuma-kun...

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:35.580
Your earlier confidence. Was that a bluff?

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:39.220
But, wait.

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:42.970
I don’t think that <i>Japan</i> #44
was made like that.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:45.430
So, what in the world is he making?

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:49.270
He wouldn’t be making fun of us,
would he?

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:53.140
Or maybe he’s unwilling to make the bread to die for, saying it’s a trade secret or something?

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:55.110
Don’t mess with us, brat!

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:58.360
We’ve come here to see your <i>Japan</i> #44 dammit!

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.740
We don’t want to see you playing
at washing some bread!

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:03.210
Yeah. Yeah!

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:07.950
Manager.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.450
It’s turned into the situation we feared after all.

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:17.130
E-Everyone in the audience,
calm down!

00:21:17.130 --> 00:21:18.210
Please calm down!

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:19.840
Yeah!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.420
Please don’t cause a disturbance!

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:25.600
Exactly. Exactly. That’s the way.

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:28.220
Cause even more of a disturbance.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:30.050
Beat those filthy cockroaches up completely.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:36.270
He’s washing the dough.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:40.820
It seems that Azuma is doing
something unexpected again.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.780
Just as expected of my rival.

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:48.910
But, the really unexpected thing is going to happen...

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:05.730
at my end.

00:22:11.850 --> 00:22:13.480
Don’t mess with us!

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:15.020
Do this seriously!

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:17.520
It’s all right like this.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:18.910
Like this...

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:23.700
Azuma Kazuma.

00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:27.990
What in... What in the world are you doing?

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:56.150
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.150 --> 00:22:58.270
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.270 --> 00:23:00.270
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:01.570
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.570 --> 00:23:04.490
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.490 --> 00:23:06.280
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:08.070
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:18.170
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.170 --> 00:23:21.050
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.050 --> 00:23:23.090
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:24.500
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:29.300
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:31.140
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:36.690
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:57.500
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.690 --> 00:24:07.710
Kanmuri Shigeru from the Central Shinjuku Branch.

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:10.010
And Azuma Kazuma, from the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:14.660
The winner of the 39th Pantasia newcomers’ battle will be decided at last!

00:24:14.660 --> 00:24:16.110
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.110 --> 00:24:18.560
Meister flying in the air!!
Who will be the winner?!

00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:19.900
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:22.690
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.060 --> 00:24:24.770
The Kaiyoushinsousui that Kanmuri developed

00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:27.990
is found at a depth of greater than 200m
underwater, where sunlight doesn’t reach.

00:24:27.990 --> 00:24:31.690
The water is rich in minerals as it
has been fermenting for 2000 years.

00:24:32.160 --> 00:24:34.170
Huh?
